# Normalize line endings for source and generated code to ensure deterministic CI
*.proto text eol=lf

# The connect-es stubs embed the whole FileDescriptorProto as one base64 string
# on a single ~9,500-character line. Marking them generated collapses them in
# review, where they are unreadable and never worth reading.
#
# It also means any two concurrent proto changes conflict here, in one hunk whose
# sides are that single line. There is no textual resolution: you cannot merge two
# base64 encodings of different schema trees, and taking --ours or --theirs looks
# like it worked while silently discarding one side's schema change.
#
#   ALWAYS resolve by regenerating:  make proto
#
# The real fix is to stop tracking these, as proto/gateon/v1/*.pb.go already are.
# That is blocked on the build: both Dockerfile and .github/ci/Dockerfile.ci build
# the dashboard in a bun stage that receives only ui/, while `buf generate` needs
# protoc-gen-es from the ui/node_modules that same stage produces. Untracking
# requires splitting into uideps -> protogen -> ui -> builder in both files, one of
# which is the release path.
ui/src/services/gen/** linguist-generated=true
*.pb.go text eol=lf
*.go text eol=lf
